   "name": null,
   "statement": "An *exact Lefschetz fibration*[^1] over $S$ consists of data $(E,\\pi,\\Omega,\\Theta,J_0,j_0)$ as follows. $E$ is a $(2n+2)$-dimensional manifold whose boundary is the union of two faces $\\partial_hE$ and $\\partial_vE$, meeting at a codimension two corner. $\\pi: E \\rightarrow S$ is a proper map with $\\partial_vE = \\pi^{-1}(\\partial S)$ (so this may be empty), and such that both $\\pi|\\partial_hE: \\partial_hE \\rightarrow S$ and $\\pi|\\partial_vE: \\partial_vE \\rightarrow \\partial S$ are smooth fibre bundles. $\\pi$ can have at most finitely many critical points, and no two may lie on the same fibre (moreover, because of the previous assumptions, they must lie in the interior of $E$).",
